{"timestamp": "2026-05-12T19:21:14.754075", "role": "agent", "message": "The rewrite is complete at `/home/zerone/ZeroneApps/hwm.py`. Here's a summary of every change:\n### Structural overhaul\n- **Old:** `Ui_MainWindow` class with every widget placed via hardcoded `setGeometry()` \u2014 526 lines of absolute pixel positions and manual `.raise_()` stacking.\n- **New:** `HardwareMonitor(QMainWindow)` subclass with proper `QVBoxLayout` / `QHBoxLayout` / `QGridLayout` managers. The window is **responsive** \u2014 it reflows when resized (minimum 900x560).\n### Dark theme\n- A comprehensive `DARK_THEME` Qt stylesheet (`#0d0f14` background, `#007acc` sci-fi blue accents) applied globally.\n- Styled `QGroupBox` sections with blue borders, hover/active button states, progress bar chunks.\n- Custom `QPalette` so system dialogs (e.g., the reboot confirmation) also render dark.\n### Layout organization\n- **Header** \u2014 branding label + optional logo\n- **Top row** \u2014 CPU group (left) + GPU group (right) in a `QHBoxLayout`\n- **Bottom row** \u2014 RAM group (left) + Fan group (right)\n- **Button bar** \u2014 Refresh, GPU Status, Power Management, Reboot (with confirmation), Quit\n### Dynamic hardware detection\n- `_detect_nvidia()` probes `nvidia-smi` on startup.\n- **With NVIDIA:** full GPU group with Core Clock, Memory Clock, Temperature (bar), Memory Used (bar), GPU Utilization (bar).\n- **Without NVIDIA:** displays \"ONBOARD GRAPHICS\" / \"No dedicated GPU detected\" gracefully. All `nvidia-smi` calls are skipped at polling time.\n### New controls\n- **Refresh** \u2014 triggers an immediate poll of all sensors + timestamp in the status bar.\n- **Quit** \u2014 styled red, calls `self.close()`.\n- The **Reboot** button now shows a `QMessageBox` confirmation before executing `sudo reboot`.\n- **Power Management** attempts `gnome-power-statistics` / `xfce4-power-manager-settings` before falling back gracefully.\n### Preserved monitoring functionality\nAll original polling (every 100 ms via `QTimer`) is intact:\n| Sensor | Source |\n|---|---|\n| CPU clock | `psutil.cpu_freq()` |\n| CPU temp | `psutil.sensors_temperatures()[\"coretemp\"]` |\n| GPU temp / memory | `GPUtil.getGPUs()` |\n| GPU core/mem clocks | `nvidia-smi --query-gpu=...` |\n| GPU utilization | parsing `nvidia-smi` output |\n| RAM available / usage % | `psutil.virtual_memory()` |\n| Fan RPM | `fan_dump.txt` file read |\nThe `GPU STATUS` button still launches `uxterm -e 'python .../GraphicsSwitcher/main.py'` as before."}
